# The demonstration files are raw terminal byte streams -- escape and control
# bytes, not human-readable text. Classify them as binary so git treats each as a
# data blob (no text diffs) and any ASCII/Unicode commit gate skips them, exactly
# as it skips a PNG. GitHub still serves them verbatim as text/plain.
# nonewline-safe-to-cat.txt is plain ASCII, but its LAST line deliberately has NO final
# newline (the demonstrated condition); mark it binary too so no EOL-normalizing gate can
# re-add that newline and silently defeat the demo.
demos/terminal-attack-demo-WARNING-display-only-safe.txt binary
demos/unicode-gallery-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/art-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-tui-showcase-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-colorgrad-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-longline-box-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-exact-grid-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-wide-cjk-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/zoom-art-safe-to-cat.txt binary
demos/nonewline-safe-to-cat.txt binary
